,title,link,text,language,family
0,Limbu people - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Limbu_people,"May 5, 2026 - The Limbu (Limbu: ᤕᤠᤰᤌᤢᤱ) are a major Sino-Tibetan ethnolinguistic group indigenous to the Himalayan region of eastern Nepal, northeastern India and western Bhutan. In India, the Limbus live in the states of Sikkim, Assam, Nagaland and northern West Bengal, i.e.",Limbu,Sino-Tibetan
1,Music of Tibet - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Music_of_Tibet,"May 6, 2026 - The music of Tibet reflects the cultural heritage of the trans-Himalayan region centered in Tibet, but also known wherever Indigenous Tibetan groups are found in Nepal, Bhutan, India and further abroad. The religious music of Tibet reflects the profound influence of Tibetan Buddhism on the culture.",Limbu,Sino-Tibetan
2,Limbus of Kanchenjunga,https://radianttreks.com/travel-guide/limbus-of-kanchenjunga/,"March 25, 2026 - Limbus has traditional pieces of music and folk dances. Limbu tribal music, like that of other Himalayan indigenous communities, is traditionally vocal. Limbu folk songs have performances and ceremonies, typically without written prompts.",Limbu,Sino-Tibetan
3,(PDF) LIMBUS: AN OUTLINE OF THEIR MUSIC AND CULTURE,https://www.academia.edu/8003804/LIMBUS_AN_OUTLINE_OF_THEIR_MUSIC_AND_CULTURE,"July 31, 2014 - Limbu religious practices are primarily rooted in Kiranti traditions, with significant influences from Tibetan Buddhism and Hinduism.",Limbu,Sino-Tibetan
