5,"Audio Recording, Music, Sino-Tibetan Languages | Library of Congress",https://loc.gov/audio/?all=true&fa=subject:music|language:sino-tibetan+languages,"Various musicians. Recorded in Vietnam. Compact disc. Notes on history and organology in English and French (11 p.) inserted in container. ... Cyomdandeta phyā phulsīs Catalog Record Only Sung in Tamang, Nepali dialect. Title from inlay sheet. Production level cataloging. ... Syombai rhāra, Guruṅga gīta ra dohorī Catalog Record Only Songs of the Gurung (Nepalese people). ... Limboo songs Catalog Record Only Limbu ...",Limbu,Sino-Tibetan
6,"Tibetan Music: Traditions, Instruments & Cultural Roots",https://windhorsetour.com/tibet-culture/tibetan-music,"April 5, 2025 - Dance and Music: Folk music is often accompanied by traditional dances, such as the Gorshey (circle dance), where people sing and dance in a circle, holding hands. Instruments: Folk music features instruments like the dranyen (a lute-like string ...",Limbu,Sino-Tibetan
7,Traditional Limbu Song | Cultural Music from Nepal,https://www.tiktok.com/@amlengshalimbu12/video/7360339446312504592,TikTok video from Amly♡ (@amlengshalimbu12),Limbu,Sino-Tibetan
8,All about Limbu: A Historically Proud Ethnic Group of Nepal - Native Nepali Stage,https://nepalnative.com/history/all-about-limbu-a-historically-proud-ethnic-group-of-nepal/,"October 31, 2025 - Each clan – or Thar – carries a distinct lineage and ancestral origins, which is reflected in the Thars such as Chemjong, Maden, Tumbahangphe and Lingden. These clans form the social backbone of Limbu society. Music and dance are an integral part of the Limbu culture.",Limbu,Sino-Tibetan
